   "plaque": "arts_grace_williams",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "Grace Williams",
   "text": "Grace Williams, born in Barry in 1906, studied in Cardiff and then at the Royal College of Music with Ralph Vaughan Williams. Her Fantasia on Welsh Nursery Tunes, from 1940, is still the piece of hers most played, and Sea Sketches from 1944 is the Bristol Channel in five movements. She wrote the score for Blue Scar, a 1949 film about a Valleys mining village, and her opera The Parlour was staged by Welsh National Opera in 1966. She died in Barry in 1977. Wales took a while to notice her. It is making up for it."
  }
